# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# SaamSaam — staging API environment overrides
# These override vars from .env (built by svc-build-env.sh)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# API
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://sm.teojordaan.com
LOG_LEVEL=debug
POSTGRES_DB=saamsaam_staging

# Telegram OFF for staging.
# The api has no TELEGRAM_MODE=off/none/disabled — config.Load accepts only
# webhook|poll and refuses anything else. The one supported disable is an EMPTY
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: main.go leaves the bot nil, logs "telegram disabled", and
# starts neither the poller nor the webhook. This empty value overrides the real
# token from .env (env_file: later file wins), so staging never calls getUpdates.
# That matters because getUpdates is single-consumer per token: staging polling
# the shared bot token would 409-fight the live api (and the real production bot).
# This is a setting, not a secret, so it belongs here in the committed .env.staging.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
